# mizan — example environment file.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local use. `.env` and every `.env.*` except this file are
# gitignored, and gate G-4 (gitleaks) fails the build if a secret is ever tracked.
#
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER. mizan ships with no credentials, and it
# runs with none — so note what a keyless run actually does, because only one of
# the two routes is live: with `MIZAN_LLM_API_KEY` left empty, a `hosted` run
# resolves to the committed transcript and every line is labelled `precomputed`
# on stdout and in the trace. That is a labelled replay, not inference.
# `model unavailable` is what a *configured* provider prints when the request
# fails, and mizan then exits non-zero. DISCLOSURE.md section 4 is the full
# disclosure.
#
# These are the only variables the code reads. `bun run check:docs` fails the
# build if this file and apps/cli/src/provider-config.ts disagree, in either
# direction — a documented variable that does nothing is as much a defect as an
# implemented one nobody can find — and it fails it again if this file
# misdescribes what the code does with them.

# ── Inference provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# hosted | scripted
#   hosted   = a live OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint (ADR-04).
#              Requires MIZAN_LLM_API_KEY. Without a key mizan falls back to
#              the committed transcript, exactly as if `scripted` were set.
#   scripted = the committed deterministic answer catalogue, labelled
#              "precomputed" in the trace and on stdout. Wins even when a key is
#              set, so an offline demo is never silently made live.
# No other value is accepted: a typo is refused with the list of valid values
# rather than quietly falling back to something.
MIZAN_PROVIDER=hosted

# The API base, not the full endpoint: mizan appends `chat/completions`.
# Optional; defaults to the value below. The host MUST be in
# PROVIDER_ALLOWED_HOSTS in apps/cli/src/provider-config.ts or the run is
# refused before any request is made (R13 / A10). The list is code, not
# configuration, so that a host cannot be added by anything that can only read
# this environment. https is required.
MIZAN_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Optional; defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
MIZAN_LLM_MODEL=replace-me

# Read from the process environment or your OS key store. Never commit a value.
# The value captured at startup is the one sent, for the whole run.
MIZAN_LLM_API_KEY=

# ── What is deliberately NOT configurable ─────────────────────────────────────
# The corpus location, the attestation file, the run ledger and the transcript
# are all fixed repo-relative paths in apps/cli/src/main.ts. There is no
# MIZAN_CORPUS_DB, no MIZAN_CORPUS_ATTESTATION, no MIZAN_TAFSIR_URL and no local
# inference mode: this build has no tafsir backend and no Ollama adapter, and
# documenting a variable for either would promise a feature that does not exist.
# tafsirLookup returns a typed "unavailable" rather than fabricating an
# explanation, and no URL changes that.
